    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/4/64486.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "I have no idea. I mean, we sat down and within five minutes, but starting the conference, The first speaker was McCarthy. He talked about how it was important that we unite, how he always said that he would put the conference first and that he would put the American people first. And he said, you know, I'm not the guy. And he just sat down. He had his whole family there with him. And everyone just said, I can't hear him. What did he say? I don't think people heard correctly or they felt like they didn't hear correctly. So it was a shock. And at this point, at that point, the speaker got up, speaker banner got up and said, we're going to postpone the speaker vote. So what happens now? I heard, you know, maybe they have another conference and pick an interim speaker. Maybe we take some more time and figure out, you know, the, I've always thought we need to figure out the what before we figure out the who. So, you know, who knows what's going to happen at this point?",
