    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "Well, I am very close, really good friends with Trey Gowdy. And it was really harmful because that comment that committee was put together to have some transparency so that the American people would know what was going on and what happened to these Americans who were killed. So it was certainly not the best comment. And he's apologized for it. Some great work was coming out of that committee and really being transparent. letting the American people know what actually happened. So I certainly hope that that committee continues to happen. I think that was a problem. But when you have a person that goes out and speaks to the public, sometimes you get some of these mistakes. Sometimes you get that. You'd rather have someone who's going to be able to get out and actually speak and apologize when they make a mistake than to have someone who is going to be completely silent and not let the American people know what's going on.",
